  answer:"Every subsequent balance is wrong, so every subsequent accrual is wrong. This is why the file is required to carry every movement without exception, and why balance checkpoints exist.<br><strong>In PCS.</strong> Periodic checkpoints in the file are compared against the balances the movements imply. A drift becomes an immediate, located mismatch instead of silent compounding.",
